{"id": "x0224", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'm going to show you how to make brisket on a pellet smoker. First things first, we' re gonna have to get our br isket ready. So let's start with the meat itself. We're gonna use some beef brisk et, which is actually one of my favorite cuts of meat. Now this piece here has been trimmed down, but if you want to trim it yourself, just remove all that excess fat and connective tissue. Once that's done, place your brisket in a large bowl and cover it with cold water. Next, add in about two tablespoons of salt per pound of br isket. This will help draw out any impurities and give us a more tender final product.Now leave it in there for about 30 minutes or so, then drain off the water and pat dry with paper towels.Now that our brisket is pre pared, we can move on to seasoning it. And for this recipe, we' re using a simple mix of salt, pepper, garlic powder, and onion powder. Just sprinkle everything over the top of the brisket and rub it in until it's evenly coated. Once that's done, set it aside while we prepare the smoke r.Now onto the smoker. Make sure your pellet smoker is clean and ready to go. If not, now would be a good time to do that.Next, load up", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
