{"id": "x0704", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'd say the most likely explanation is A, it ate more food. P uppies grow mainly by consuming milk from their mother or eating food. If one pup py ate more than the others, it' d naturally be heavier after six months. While activity level might affect muscle tone, it doesn' t directly add much weight. Drinking water helps with hydration but not much with size. And sunlight isn' t a major factor in weight gain for young puppies. So more food is the key difference.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0712", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A chemical change happens when dough bake s in an oven. When dough bakes, the heat causes a reaction that changes its chemical makeup, turning it into bread. The other options are physical changes because they don't alter the substance's chemical structure.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0720", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 32, "onset_chunk": 31, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Based on the experiment described, which seeds produced the tallest plants could be answered at the end of the month. All the conditions were controlled except for the type of seed used. So after a month, measuring the height of each plant would show which variety grew the tallest under those specific conditions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
