{"id": "x0776", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, me tamorph osis. While trees and f rogs have different life cycle s, both experience metamorph osis in some form. For frogs, this means a transition from tadpole to adult. In the case of certain tree species, like some con ifers or specific types that undergo significant changes in structure over time, metamorphosis can be loosely applied as a broad term for transformation, though it's more commonly associated with animals. So while growth and dorm ancy are also part of their cycles, metamorphosis is the shared stage most accurately fitting both contexts.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0784", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest organ in the human body is C, skin. It covers our entire surface and protect s us from harmful elements like UV rays and bacteria.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0792", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'd expect to find the formation of a cell plate in Vol vox but not in amoeb as. This process occurs during cell division in Volvox, which involves specialized structures like cell plates for dividing into new units. Amoebas, on the other hand, typically use cytokinesis without forming a distinct cell plate.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
